   "source": [
    "# Smart MCQ Solver Challenge\n",
    "\n",
    "## Project Overview\n",
    "\n",
    "The goal of this project is to rank the three most probable answers for each multiple-choice question containing five candidate options (A–E).\n",
    "\n",
    "The competition is evaluated using Mean Average Precision at 3 (MAP@3), which rewards placing the correct answer higher in the predicted ranking.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Models Used\n",
    "\n",
    "1. **Custom MLP** — trained from scratch using TF-IDF/SVD-based features\n",
    "2. **MiniLM** — pretrained transformer-based model\n",
    "3. **DeBERTa-v3-small + LoRA** — pretrained transformer fine-tuned efficiently using LoRA\n",
    "\n",
    "The final predictions are generated from model outputs using a validation-based weighted ensemble."
   ]
  },
