    "## 3. Validation Strategy\n",
    "\n",
    "Builds an `opt_key` from the concatenated option text (the five answer choices, in order) and splits with `GroupShuffleSplit` grouped on that key, so every group of near-duplicate questions stays entirely on one side of the 85/15 split.\n",
    "\n",
    "Section 5 found 210 option-sets shared by more than one training row — these are reworded duplicates of the same underlying question. A plain random split could put two copies of the same question on opposite sides of train/validation, which would let a model \"cheat\" by memorizing rather than generalizing, and would make the validation MAP@3 look better than it really is. Grouping on `opt_key` closes that leak.\n"
