    "## 4. Evaluation Metric — MAP@3\n",
    "\n",
    "Implements MAP@3 directly from the ranked option scores, plus a helper that turns ranked scores into the `\"X Y Z\"` label string the submission file expects.\n",
    "\n",
    "MAP@3 isn't built into scikit-learn, and it's the competition's actual scoring metric, so every model in this notebook is compared on it directly rather than on a proxy.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Worked example:** if the true answer is `B` and a model ranks its top three as `[B, A, C]`, the reciprocal rank is `1/1 = 1.0` (full credit). If it ranks `[A, B, C]`, the reciprocal rank is `1/2 = 0.5`. If `B` isn't in the top three at all, the score for that row is `0`. MAP@3 is just the mean of that reciprocal rank across all rows.\n",
    "\n"
   ]
  },
