    "## 5. Model 1 — Custom MLP\n",
    "\n",
    "The project requires one model built entirely from scratch, with no pretrained weights anywhere in it.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Feature representation:** the prompt and each of the five options are embedded with TF-IDF followed by truncated SVD — a classical, non-pretrained embedding (the vocabulary and the SVD projection are both fit only on the training split). For each option, four feature blocks are concatenated: the prompt embedding, the option embedding, their element-wise product, and their absolute difference, plus a scalar cosine similarity — giving the model both the raw representations and explicit interaction features to work with.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Architecture:** a deeper MLP scorer than a single hidden layer, so the model has enough capacity to combine those interaction features non-linearly, while staying small enough to train from scratch on ~1,700 rows without overfitting immediately:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "Input (513-d)\n",
    "  -> Linear -> ReLU -> Dropout(0.3)\n",
    "  -> Linear -> ReLU -> Dropout(0.3)\n",
    "  -> Linear -> ReLU\n",
    "  -> Linear -> 1 score\n",
    "```\n",
    "The same scorer is applied independently to each of the five (prompt, option) feature vectors, giving five scores per question."
   ]
