    "### Key Takeaways — Model 2\n",
    "\n",
    "- **What did we build?** Nothing trained — a zero-shot scoring pipeline built entirely on a frozen pretrained sentence encoder.\n",
    "- **Why did we build it?** It's pretrained model, and it isolates how much of the task a general-purpose semantic model can solve with no task-specific training at all.\n",
    "- **What does it learn/use?** Pretrained MiniLM sentence embeddings; no weights are updated on this dataset.\n",
    "- **What metric did it achieve?** Validation MAP@3 = 0.3811.\n",
    "- **Strengths/limitations:** Captures broad semantic similarity with zero training cost, but has no way to learn this dataset's specific answer patterns — it is clearly the weakest of the three models on this task."
