   "source": [
    "## 10. Model 3 — DeBERTa-v3-small + LoRA\n",
    "\n",
    "### MCQ formulation\n",
    "Each question with prompt `P` and options `A`-`E` is expanded into five candidate (prompt, option) pairs:\n",
    "\n",
    "```\n",
    "(P, A), (P, B), (P, C), (P, D), (P, E)\n",
    "```\n",
    "\n",
    "`AutoModelForMultipleChoice` encodes all five pairs and produces **one logit per choice**. The five logits are softmax-normalized into probabilities, ranked, and the top three are kept.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why DeBERTa?\n",
    "DeBERTa-v3-small is a transformer encoder pretrained with disentangled attention (content and position are encoded separately), which tends to give stronger contextual representations than a plain BERT-style encoder at a similar parameter count — useful here because many questions require actually parsing what the prompt is asking, not just matching keywords.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Why LoRA?\n",
    "Full fine-tuning would update all ~142M parameters of the base model. LoRA instead freezes the pretrained weights and injects small trainable low-rank adapter matrices into the attention projections (`query_proj`, `key_proj`, `value_proj`), plus keeps the pooler/classifier head trainable. This drastically cuts the number of trainable parameters and the compute/memory needed to fine-tune, while still letting the model adapt to this specific task.\n",
    "\n",
    "**Actual parameter counts from this run:** 812,545 trainable out of 142,708,226 total (**0.5694%** trainable) — from `model3.print_trainable_parameters()` below.\n",
    "\n",
    "### Training\n",
    "- **Tokenizer:** DeBERTa-v3-small's own tokenizer, `(prompt, option)` pairs, truncated/padded to `max_length=256`.\n",
    "- **Batch size:** 8 (train), 16 (eval).\n",
    "- **Learning rate:** 2e-4.\n",
    "- **Epochs:** 3.\n",
    "- **Optimizer / trainer:** Hugging Face `Trainer`, with a custom `DataCollatorForMultipleChoice` that reshapes the 5-choices-per-question batches correctly.\n",
    "- **LoRA config:** rank `r=8`, `alpha=16`, `dropout=0.05`, applied to the attention projections.\n",
    "- **Validation:** evaluated every epoch on the same held-out split as Models 1 and 2; `metric_for_best_model=\"map3\"` so the best checkpoint on validation MAP@3 is kept."
   ]
  },
