    "## 12. Ensemble\n",
    "\n",
    "Grid-searches ensemble weights `(w1, w2, w3)` over the three models' validation probabilities to maximize validation MAP@3, then applies the winning weights to the test-set probabilities.\n",
    "\n",
    "The three models make different kinds of errors — Model 1 relies on lexical/statistical overlap, Model 2 on generic semantic similarity, Model 3 on task-fine-tuned contextual reasoning — so a weighted combination can correct some of one model's mistakes with another's strength, if their errors aren't too correlated.\n",
    "\n",
    "Weights are searched on a 0.1-resolution grid over `w1 + w2 + w3 = 1`, choosing the combination that maximizes MAP@3 **on the validation split only** — the test set is never used to pick weights.\n"
   ]
  },
