    "## 15. Limitations\n",
    "\n",
    "- **Small dataset:** ~1,700 training rows after the validation split is not a lot of data to fine-tune a transformer or train an MLP from scratch — both Model 1 and Model 3's numbers should be read as indicative, not as a tight estimate of generalization.\n",
    "- **Single validation split:** results come from one 85/15 grouped split rather than cross-validation, so the reported metrics carry some split-dependent variance.\n",
    "- **Duplicate questions:** Section 5/6 showed the dataset contains many reworded duplicate questions; the grouped split prevents leakage between train and validation, but does not remove the underlying duplication in the data itself.\n",
    "- **Limited fine-tuning budget:** Model 3 was trained for 3 epochs at a fixed LoRA configuration — no hyperparameter search was run, so its reported performance is a single configuration's result, not a ceiling on what fine-tuning could achieve."
   ]
  },
