    "## 17. Final Conclusion\n",
    "\n",
    "Three models were built and compared honestly on the same validation split: a from-scratch TF-IDF/SVD MLP (MAP@3=0.6189), a zero-shot pretrained MiniLM model (MAP@3=0.3811), and a LoRA-fine-tuned DeBERTa-v3-small (MAP@3=0.5091). **Model 1 performed best on this validation split**, ahead of the fine-tuned transformer, with the zero-shot pretrained model clearly weakest — a reminder that \"more pretrained\" doesn't automatically mean \"better\" on a small, specific dataset without task-specific training. The ensemble combines all three based on validation-tuned weights (Section 12), with no lookup or answer-matching step anywhere in the final prediction path."
